message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "ldct-io: read, reconstruct and measure real CT projection data (DICOM-CT-PD)"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Institute-of-One/ldct-io"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22723943"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22723944"
    description: >-
      The archived version 0.1.0, the release behind the real-scanner arm of the J. Imaging
      manuscript jimaging-4539482. Cite this one to pin the code; the DOI above always
      resolves to the latest version.
abstract: >-
  Reads DICOM-CT-PD projection data as distributed by The Cancer Imaging Archive, restores
  acquisition order from headers rather than filenames, rebins helical fan-beam projections
  to single slices, reconstructs them by filtered backprojection with a selectable
  apodisation, and measures the physical quantities that task-based image quality is built
  on. It exists so that a measurement made on a real scanner can be re-derived from the
  archived projections rather than taken on trust.
